  "notes": "Colour semantics carry the whole UI. Cascade Harvest shifts are pale green chips (#e2f1e9/#2e7d5b), Whisker Haven shifts are pale amber (#fbeedb/#9a5b13), and the standing tutoring commitment is a solid blue chip (#2f5fa6). Booked shifts are solid dark green or solid red with a ✓, and clashing shifts are pale red with a red outline. Days blocked by personal commitments (Spokane work trip, Family weekend) get diagonal hatched-stripe gradient backgrounds and a small bold tag next to the date. 'Holiday week' tags are in brown. Wednesdays show the assumed recurring 'Climbing, 5:00–10:00 pm (assumed)' as muted text in the cell. The left sidebar acts as a decision-support rail: an hours meter against a user-set ceiling, conflict cards with concrete fixes ('Move to Sat, Dec 5…'), and a 'Best fit' bundle with one button to swap and book. The Monthly ceiling box has a dashed border. There are no shadows; everything uses 1px borders and 6–12px radii. Live checks: tabs switch to a filterable shift table, and clicking a shift chip opens a right-hand detail drawer over a scrim with a 'Book this shift' button."
